  "problem": {
    "statement": "JIRA Issue: DOC-3193\n\nTitle: Commerce Eligibility Example Rework for Role Targeting\n\nDescription:\n## Problem\n\nThe customer eligibility customization page demonstrates a custom eligibility evaluator but does not use member roles. With v31.3.0 introducing native role support, the eligibility example should be reworked to showcase a practical role-based scenario (e.g., \"Premium members receive a discount\").\n\n## Description\n\nRework the custom eligibility example in `customer-eligibility-customization.md` to demonstrate role-based discount targeting using member roles.\n\n### Scenario\n\n> **\"Premium members get a 15% discount\"** — A custom eligibility evaluator that checks whether the current member has the \"Premium\" role and, if so, qualifies them for a promotion.\n\n### Changes\n\n  * **Rework the custom eligibility evaluator example** to inject `RoleManager<ApplicationRole>` or `UserManager<ApplicationUser>` and check the current user's roles\n  * **Use **`User.IsInRole(\"Premium\")` or `UserManager.IsInRoleAsync()` for the eligibility check\n  * **Update the corresponding code sample** in the codesamples project\n  * **Keep the overall page structure** — this is a rework of the existing example, not a new page\n\n### Example Pattern\n\n``` csharp\npublic class PremiumMemberEligibilityEvaluator : ICustomerEligibilityEvaluator\n{\n    private readonly IHttpContextAccessor httpContextAccessor;\n\n    public PremiumMemberEligibilityEvaluator(IHttpContextAccessor httpContextAccessor)\n    {\n        this.httpContextAccessor = httpContextAccessor;\n    }\n\n    public Task<bool> IsEligible(CustomerEligibilityContext context)\n    {\n        var user = httpContextAccessor.HttpContext?.User;\n\n        if (user?.Identity?.IsAuthenticated != true)\n        {\n            return Task.FromResult(false);\n        }\n\n        return Task.FromResult(user.IsInRole(\"Premium\"));\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Promotion Setup Context\n\nThe documentation should note:\n\n  * The \"Premium\" member role is created in **Members → Member Roles** in the admin\n  * Members assigned the \"Premium\" role automatically qualify for promotions using this evaluator\n  * This pattern works for any role name — not limited to \"Premium\"\n\n## Affected Files\n\n|Action|File Path|Details|\n|:-:|:-:|:-:|\n|UPDATE |`src/_documentation/_documentation/developers-and-admins/digital-commerce-setup/promotions/customer-eligibility-customization.md` |Rework eligibility example with role-based targeting |\n|UPDATE |`src/_code/src/CodeSamples/DigitalCommerce/Promotions/` |Update corresponding code samples |\n\n\n## Technical Context\n\n### [ASP.NET](http://ASP.NET) Identity Role Claims\n\n  * When `ApplicationRole`/`ApplicationRoleStore` are configured, [ASP.NET](http://ASP.NET) Identity adds role claims to the `ClaimsPrincipal`\n  * `User.IsInRole(\"RoleName\")` works out of the box for checking membership\n  * `UserManager<ApplicationUser>.IsInRoleAsync(user, \"RoleName\")` for server-side checks outside HTTP context\n\n### Source References\n\n  * DancingGoat examples in `CMSSolution/DancingGoat/` demonstrate role-based patterns\n  * `ApplicationRoleStore` manages the `IRoleStore<TRole>` mapping to `MemberRoleInfo`\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n  * [ ] Customer eligibility example reworked to use member role checking\n  * [ ] Example uses `User.IsInRole()` or equivalent pattern\n  * [ ] Promotion setup context mentioned (creating role in admin, assigning to members)\n  * [ ] Codesamples updated to match documentation examples\n  * [ ] Existing page structure preserved (this is an example rework, not a new page)\n  * [ ] Documentation builds without errors\n  * [ ] Codesamples compile\n\n## Dependencies\n\n  * JIRA-01 (developer member roles page) — cross-link for role setup\n  * JIRA-02 (auth pages NoOp deprecation) — Program.cs must register real role types\n\n## Notes\n\n  * The exact code sample structure in `src/_code/src/CodeSamples/DigitalCommerce/Promotions/` should be reviewed before implementation to understand the current eligibility example pattern\n\nLabels: commerce, documentation, membership-roles, xperience-by-kentico\n\nPriority: Not set\n\nWas this page helpful?: Helpful\n\n⚠️ REMINDER: This task involves the code samples project (ralph-codesamples skill). The coder subagent will bootstrap the project with xpversion=31.3.0-b558778 before research begins. Build with `npm run codesamples:build` before committing any .cs files.\n⚠️ REMINDER: Admin UI interaction is enabled for this task. The coder verifies admin access; the writer can create admin objects via Playwright (see ralph-codesamples-adminui skill)."
  },
