k file structure and `tasks.json` format\n- `references/revision-mode.md` — planning revision fixes from reviewer feedback\n\n#### **File 4: ralph-workflow Skill**\n**Path:** `/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/shared/skills/workflow/docs/ralph-workflow/SKILL.md`\n\nRouter skill for Ralph documentation workflow phases:\n- **Standard Workflow (8 phases):** Setup → Research → Write → Review → Commit → PR → Handoff → Exit\n- **Revision Workflow (7 phases):** Setup → Fix → Review → Commit → Handoff → Exit\n- Routes to correct phase reference files in `references/`\n- Control files: `state.md` (phase tracking) and `ralph-planner/tasks.json` (task lifecycle)\n\n#### **File 5: ralph-codesamples shared include**\n**Path:** `/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/shared/agent-includes/ralph-docs/ralph-codesamples.md`\n\nAgent-include partial defining Code Samples task requirements for Researcher, Writer, Validator, Reviewer, and Coder roles:\n- Code samples project at `src/_code/src/`\n- Researcher: explore samples, find `code_link` usage, identify gaps\n- Writer: read researcher findings, create/update `.cs` files, add `code_link` tags\n- Validator: verify `code_link` paths, build passes, inclusion markers\n- Reviewer: API correctness, `code_link` accuracy, build status\n- Coder: bootstrap workflow with specific version target\n\n---\n\n### 3. **AGENT DEFINITIONS (ralph-planner)**\n\n#### **File 6: Ralph Planner Agent (ralph-docs profile)**\n**Path:** `/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/profiles/ralph-docs/agents/ralph.ralph-planner.agent.md`\n\n**Complete ralph-planner definition** for the documentation workflow. Key sections:\n\n- **Description:** Planning sub-agent that breaks research artifacts into ordered task files for headless writer execution\n- **Model:** claude-opus-4.6\n- **Result codes:** `planned` (tasks created), `blocked` (cannot produce reliable breakdown)\n- **Required skills to load:**\n  - `ralph-task-planning` (core decomposition)\n  - `xperience-documentation` (page placement decisions)\n  - `ralph-codesamples` (when task touches code samples)\n  - Others: `ralph-research-guide`, `ralph-ralphchives`, etc.\n  \n- **Input sources:**\n  - Standard mode: researcher's `status.json` + all artifacts in `artifacts` array\n  - Revision mode: `state.md` feedback, reviewer findings, writer artifacts, existing `tasks.json`\n  \n- **Task design rules:**\n  - Small, reviewable tasks over large batches\n  - Minimize file overlap\n  - Dependencies only when necessary\n  - Headless execution (no human checkpoints)\n  - Write for automatic execution\n  \n- **Required artifacts:**\n  1. `output.md` — planning summary\n  2. `tasks.json` — machine-readable ordered task index with format:\n     ```json\n     {\n       \"mode\": \"standard|revision\",\n       \"task_count\": N,\n       \"tasks\": [\n         {\n           \"id\": \"TASK-01\",\n           \"title\": \"...\",\n           \"path\": \"ralph-planner/task-01-slug.md\",\n           \"lifecycle\": \"not_processed\",\n           \"attempt\": 0,\n           \"depends_on\": [],\n           \"files\": [\"src/_documentation/...\"],\n           \"type\": \"documentation|codesamples|mixed|release notes\"\n         }\n       ]\n     }\n     ```\n  3. Task files: `task-01-<slug>.md`, `task-02-<slug>.md`, etc. with sections:\n     - Objective\n     - Scope (files changed/created)\n     - Constraints\n     - Execution Steps\n     - Acceptance Criteria\n     - Reviewer Focus (Technical/Style/IA)\n     - Follow-ups (deferred work only)\n\n#### **File 7: Ralph Planner Agent (ralph-vscode profile)**\n**Path:** `/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/profiles/ralph-vscode/agents/ralph.ralph-planner.agent.md`\n\nVariant for VS Code extension codebase (TypeScript project):\n- **Description:** Planning sub-agent for `kentico-docs-autocomplete-vscode` extension\n- **Model:** claude-opus-4.6\n- **Result codes:** `planned`, `verified`, `gaps_found`, `blocked`\n- **Architecture focus:** definition-driven patterns (tag definitions, header definitions, YAML definitions)\n- **Additional input sources:** analyst plan at `{{ artifactDir }}/ralph-analyst/output.md`, explorer artifacts\n- **Verification mode:** Re-read analyst plan, compare against implemented state, detect missing/incomplete work\n- **Key file areas:** `src/definitions/`, `src/logic/`, `grammars/`\n\n---\n\n### 4. **TASK-PLANNING REFERENCE FILES**\n\n#### **File 8: Task Boundaries Reference**\n**Path:** `/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/shared/skills/tasks/ralph-task-planning/references/task-boundaries.md`\n\nGuidance on task granularity:\n- **Prefer one task when:** single file changes, same documentation neighborhood, same research artifact, shared reviewer concerns\n- **Split tasks when:** different doc sections, page creation vs navigation, docs vs code samples, release notes, admin UI\n- **Dependency rules:** only use dependencies for page creation prerequisites, codesamples→docs citations, frontmatter depending on content files\n- **Deferred work:** defer items in `_guides`, outside scope, needing different workflow, lacking evidence\n\n#### **File 9: Task Files Format Reference**\n**Path:** `/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/shared/skills/tasks/ralph-task-planning/references/task-files.md`\n\nDefines `tasks.json` shape and task file markdown template:\n- `tasks.json` structure with `mode`, `task_count`, `tasks` array\n- Each task object has: `id`, `title`, `path`, `depends_on`, `files`, `type`\n- Task file markdown format with sections for Objective, Scope, Constraints, Execution Steps, Acceptance Criteria, Reviewer Focus, Follow-ups\n- Quality bar: fresh writer can execute without chat history, reviewers know what to audit, coherent work slice, explicit deferred work\n\n#### **File 10: Revision Mode Reference**\n**Path:** `/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/shared/skills/tasks/ralph-task-planning/references/revision-mode.md`\n\nGuidance for planning revision fixes from reviewer feedback:\n- **Revision goals:** preserve approved work, keep loop narrow, avoid reopening unrelated tasks, map cleanly to findings\n- **Reuse vs split:** reuse task shape if feedback affects one task only; split for navigation/frontmatter, codesamples isolation, independent fixes\n- **Approved work:** stable unless directly reopened\n- **Conversion:** cluster findings by file ownership, keep together only when one change resolves all\n- **Deferred:** belongs in `_guides`, needs different workflow, requires wider restructure, evidence too weak\n\n---\n\n### 5. **ARTIFACTS FROM DOC-3193 TASK**\n\n#### **File 11: Ralph Planner Status (from run-analyzer)**\n**Path:** `/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/.ralph/tasks/DOC-3193/artifacts/run-analyzer/ralph-planner/status.json`\n\nCompleted analysis of a ralph-planner run:\n```json\n{\n  \"agent\": \"run-analyzer\",\n  \"task_id\": \"DOC-3193\",\n  \"status\": \"completed\",\n  \"result\": \"analyzed\",\n  \"summary\": \"ralph-planner: pass — clean 3m56s execution, 3-task breakdown with correct dependencies, zero errors, full artifact compliance. Minor: consider Sonnet over Opus, enrich dispatch prompt with trigger params.\",\n  \"artifacts\": [\"run-analyzer/ralph-planner/output.md\"],\n  \"next_hint\": null,\n  \"iteration\": 1\n}\n```\n\n#### **File 12: Ralph Planner Extraction Report (from subagent-mapper)**\n**Path:** `/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/.ralph/tasks/DOC-3193/artifacts/subagent-mapper/subagents/ralph-planner.md`\n\nDetailed execution report on ralph-planner run:\n- **Model:** claude-opus-4.6\n- **Span:** lines 18567–21054 of task processing\n- **Metrics:** 64 tool calls, 19 LLM turns, ~high token usage\n- **Tool sequence:** report_intent → view researcher output → bash analysis → create task files → sql tracking → generate plan\n- **Errors:** None\n- **Result:** `planned`, `status: completed`\n- **Summary:** \"3 tasks planned: TASK-01 reworks code samples (VIP→Premium), TASK-02 updates docs page (depends TASK-01), TASK-03 adds glossary entry.\"\n\n#### **File 13: DOC-3193 Artifacts Manifest**\n**Path:** `/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/.ralph/tasks/DOC-3193/artifacts/manifest.json`\n\nAudit log of all subagent runs for the task:\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"timestamp\": \"2026-03-12T21:26:05Z\",\n    \"agent\": \"subagent-mapper\",\n    \"artifacts\": [\"subagent-mapper/output.md\", \"subagent-mapper/subagents/...\"],\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"result\": \"mapped\",\n    \"iteration\": 1\n  },\n  // ... (2 more entries for run-analyzer iterations)\n]\n```\n\n---\n\n## Key Takeaways\n\n**The ralph-planner workflow:**\n\n1. **Receives input:** Researcher `status.json` + artifacts OR revision feedback\n2. **Loads core skills:** `ralph-task-planning`, `xperience-documentation`, and contextual skills\n3. **Produces artifacts:**\n   - `output.md` — planning narrative\n   - `tasks.json` — machine-readable task index\n   - Individual task markdown files\n   - `status.json` — structured result (completed/failed, result code, summary, artifacts)\n   - Appends to `manifest.json` for audit trail\n4. **Execution mode:** Fully headless, no human checkpoints, task files self-contained\n5. **For revision:** Clusters reviewer findings by file ownership, preserves approved work, defers work out of scope\n6. **Task design:** Small reviewable units, explicit dependencies, clear reviewer focus per task\n\nAll referenced agent-includes and skills are shared partials that can be rendered inline into planner prompts via the `{% render %}` liquid tag and `{% section %}` wrapper pattern.",
